  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Study: a clip launcher and looper (clip slots, scenes, quantized launch, a loop pedal), rebuilt with Phase 4's tools.\n\nThree tracks with two clip slots each. A slot is one Clip Slot block: press its button and its clip starts on the next bar line; launching the other slot on its track (wired into `release`) or the track's Stop button ends it on the bar. Its card is the slot's button with a light for armed (waiting for the bar) and one for playing. A scene button launches a row. The Looper is one node: Record starts a loop at the next bar and ends it at the bar after the next press, then plays it round; Overdub layers more on top, and Undo takes the last layer off. In a render the demo launches scene 1 at the start and scene 2 at bar 5. The Session panel is the grid: a column per track, a row per scene, the stop buttons, and a channel strip per track.\n\nWhat a launcher has that this can't: follow actions, and recording a loop whose length sets the tempo. Read docs/GAPS.md."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -680.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            270.0
          ]
        }
      },
